Theorem RL-14: non-escaping headerless stack allocation (Locality <= FunctionLocal, Unique)

  Preconditions:
    - RL-14 governs headerless stack promotion per Annex E §AIMS Stack
      Promotion: non-escaping allocations (Locality <= FunctionLocal AND
      Uniqueness = Unique) with fixed size SHALL be stack-allocated via
      alloca with NO RC header and NO RC ops; stack dealloc at scope exit.
      Owned reference-type FIELDS receive explicit RcDec in REVERSE
      declaration order at scope exit (VF-1 exempts these field-drop
      Project+RcDec from DecOnBorrowed).
    - Signature ArcFunction x AimsStateMap -> ArcFunction per
      the canonical proof notation:264; discharged against the sec-01
      Realization.proof sorry obligation.
    - DP-8 (is_local) <=> Locality IN {BlockLocal, FunctionLocal}. Uniqueness
      = Unique is load-bearing: a MaybeShared headerless stack value crashes
      on IsShared (DP-4), so non-unique locals route to RL-14a (immortal
      header) instead.
    - Shipped: realize/project_escape.rs (escape-driven field RcDec) +
      realize/decide.rs (Locality consumption); repr.md sec-RH-3
      heap-vs-stack classification.
    - depends-on sec-05: DP-8 (is_local) soundness.

  Soundness property:
    Forall fixed-size value v:

      (P1) Strategy decision: RL-14 selects a headerless stack allocation iff
           is_local(v) (Locality <= FunctionLocal) AND Uniqueness(v) = Unique
           AND v is fixed-size. A non-unique local routes to RL-14a; a
           dynamic-size local routes to RL-15; an escaping value routes to
           RL-16.

      (P2) RC soundness: a headerless stack value carries no RC header and
           emits no RC ops on itself — it cannot be shared (Unique) and
           cannot escape the frame (local), so it is deallocated by the stack
           frame at scope exit. Its Owned heap-reference FIELDS receive
           field-level RcDec at scope exit (reverse declaration order),
           releasing the children exactly once.

    RL-14 refines plain ARC: plain ARC heap-allocates every reference value
    with a full RC header; RL-14 eliminates the header AND every RC op when
    the lattice proves the value is local + unique + fixed-size.

  Proof obligation:
    Constructive discharge by the case_analysis engine via finite
    enumeration of the Locality x Uniqueness x size strategy grid.

    Part (P1/P2) — strategy grid:
      blocklocal_unique_fixed_headerless -> HeaderlessStack
      functionlocal_unique_fixed_headerless -> HeaderlessStack
      local_maybeshared_immortal_header -> ImmortalHeaderStack (RL-14a)
      local_unique_dynamic_bump -> BumpAlloc (RL-15)
      heapescaping_heap -> Heap (RL-16)
      Coverage gate: 5 strategy decisions. Negative-direction witness: a
      MaybeShared local must NOT be headerless (would crash on IsShared) —
      asserted.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (PRIMARY — section_08::verify_rl14_headerless_stack;
        Locality x Uniqueness x size strategy enumeration; emits Fail on a
        wrong strategy or an unsound headerless selection)
      rc_counting (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)
      refinement (SECONDARY — gracious-accept per the coverage-manifest RL
        row)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_08 case_analysis engine discharges RL-14 via the Locality x Uniqueness x size strategy grid (headerless stack only for local+Unique+fixed; non-unique -> RL-14a immortal header; dynamic -> RL-15 bump; escaping -> RL-16 heap) with a negative-direction witness rejecting a headerless MaybeShared local, grounded in the shipped realize/project_escape.rs field-RcDec + repr.md RH-3 classification
